<title>USA: TCF Financial rescinds stock buyback.</title>
<headline>TCF Financial rescinds stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>TCF Financial Corp said Tuesday it formally rescinded its stock repurchase program in connection with its pending merger with Winthrop Resources, a Minneapolis-based leasing company.</p>
<p>The merger will be treated as a pooling of interests for accounting purposes.</p>
<p>TCF said it had 79,788 shares remaining unpurchased in its current five percent stock repurchase program of December 1995. Its board also had authorized on January 20, 1997 the repurchase of an additional five percent, or 1.7 million shares.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
</text>
